<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-BRITISH LIONS BEAT SOUTH AFRICA 25-16.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-BRITISH LIONS BEAT SOUTH AFRICA 25-16.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British Lions beat South Africa 25-16 (halftime 8-9) in the first match of their three test series at Newlands on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>British Lions - Tries: Matt Dawson, Alan Tait. Penalties: Neil Jenkins (5).</p>
<p>South Africa - Tries: Os du Randt, Russell Bennett. Penalties: Edrich Lubbe, Henry Honiball.</p>
</text>
